<PageTitle>Home</PageTitle>

<h1>Welcome!</h1>


<p>This page will help you get started on how to use the spreadsheet.</p>

<p> Get started by selecting a cell, entering some contents into the input box labeled "Contents", and hitting 
    "Enter" to display the data in the spreadsheet grid.
</p>
    
<p> The valid contents are a string (a word or a letter), a number, or a formula. A formula is identified by the 
    "=" at the beginning of the input. Without the "=", your formula would be processed as a string.
</p>

<p> The value of a cell is the result from evaluating the contents. It will be the same as the contents if the 
    contents is a number or word, but when the contents is a formula, the value will be the result from evaluating 
    the formula.
</p>

<p> If you enter a formula that when evaluating results in an error, (for example, you enter "=A1+2" but A1 
    contains the word "hello"), then the value is "Formula Error".
</p>

<p> If you input an invalid formula, then you get an error message, and your spreadsheet will not be changed. Invalid 
    formulas occur when you use invalid tokens within the formula, refer to an invalid cell name, or refer to a cell
    that will cause a cycle (for example, A1 contains "=B1+2" but B1 contains "=A1+2" which causes a cycle). The only
    valid tokens allowed are +, -, *, /, (, ), a cell name, and any number (including integers, decimals, and 
    numbers in scientific notation). Negative numbers are NOT allowed, but the formula can evaluate to a negative 
    number.
</p>

<p> UNIQUE FEATURE: You can customize your spreadsheet by changing the colors of your cells. By default, all cell 
    colors are white. You can change the cell colors by clicking on the box next to "Choose Cell Color:" and 
    selecting a color from the color picker.
</p>

<p> You can save your spreadsheet by clicking on the "Save" button. Saving your spreadsheet saves all of the data, 
    including the cell colors. Note that if you refresh the page without saving your spreadsheet, you will lose 
    that spreadsheet.
</p>

<p> You can also load an existing spreadsheet into the page by clicking on the "Load" button and selecting a file that
    you want to load. If you try to load a file that does not translate to a valid spreadsheet, the current 
    spreadsheet will not be changed.
</p>